  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I appears to interact with SNB-78 through multiple distinct but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that the compound targets different members of the SDR family and microtubule-associated proteins, which in turn are targeted by various compounds, including N-Methyltyramine and 4-Fluorobenzoic acid, tridec-2-ynyl ester. These compounds are known to modulate SNB-78, indicating a potential role for Sasanquasaponin I in influencing SNB-78 activity through different molecular mechanisms. The shared target of SNB-78 across these pathways implies that Sasanquasaponin I may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these proteins, potentially through inhibition or regulation of metabolic or structural pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Sasanquasaponin I could act as a modulator of SNB-78, though further validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism and therapeutic relevance.",
